# Testing & Quality Assurance Rules
# CBRICENHO Chatbot - XP Testing Practices

## Test-Driven Development (TDD) Workflow

### Red-Green-Refactor Cycle
```
1. RED: Write a failing test first
2. GREEN: Write minimum code to pass the test
3. REFACTOR: Clean up the code while keeping tests green
```

### TDD Example for Fulfillment Handler
```javascript
// Step 1: RED - Write failing test
describe('AppointmentHandler', () => {
  describe('validateAppointmentDate', () => {
    it('should reject dates more than 7 days in the future', () => {
      const futureDate = new Date();
      futureDate.setDate(futureDate.getDate() + 10);
      
      expect(() => validateAppointmentDate(futureDate))
        .toThrow('La fecha debe estar dentro de los próximos 7 días');
    });
  });
});

// Step 2: GREEN - Write minimum code
const validateAppointmentDate = (date) => {
  const maxDate = new Date();
  maxDate.setDate(maxDate.getDate() + 7);
  
  if (date > maxDate) {
    throw new Error('La fecha debe estar dentro de los próximos 7 días');
  }
  return true;
};

// Step 3: REFACTOR - Clean up
const validateAppointmentDate = (date, maxDays = 7) => {
  const maxAllowedDate = addDays(new Date(), maxDays);
  
  if (isAfter(date, maxAllowedDate)) {
    throw new ValidationError(ERRORS.DATE_TOO_FAR, { maxDays });
  }
  return true;
};
```

