## Unit Testing Standards

### File Naming Convention
```
src/
├── services/
│   ├── appointment.service.js
│   └── appointment.service.test.js
├── handlers/
│   ├── faq.handler.js
│   └── faq.handler.test.js
```

### Test Structure (AAA Pattern)
```javascript
describe('ServiceName', () => {
  describe('methodName', () => {
    it('should [expected behavior] when [condition]', async () => {
      // Arrange - Set up test data and mocks
      const mockInput = { /* ... */ };
      const mockDependency = jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(/* ... */);
      
      // Act - Execute the code under test
      const result = await serviceMethod(mockInput);
      
      // Assert - Verify the results
      expect(result).toEqual(expectedOutput);
      expect(mockDependency).toHaveBeenCalledWith(/* ... */);
    });
  });
});
```

### Required Test Coverage by Module

| Module | Min Coverage | Critical Paths |
|--------|-------------|----------------|
| handlers/ | 90% | All intent handlers |
| services/ | 95% | Business logic |
| utils/ | 80% | Helper functions |
| models/ | 70% | Schema validations |

